# Experiment 2 (geometry) — API keys
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the keys you actually need.
# `.env` is gitignored at the repo root; never commit it.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# The config cell resolves a key in this order:
#   1. an exported environment variable
#   2. a .env file — the notebook's own folder, then up to two parents
#   3. a Colab secret
# A single .env here, or in exp2_phase2/, covers every model folder below it.
#
# Only the key named by the selected preset is required. Pick the model with
# USE_MODEL in the config cell; each preset declares its own key_env.

# ---- USE_MODEL = "gpt-4.1-mini" -----------------------------------------
# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# ---- USE_MODEL = "deepseek-v4-pro" | "deepseek-v4-flash" | "deepseek-chat"
# https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys        (endpoint: https://api.deepseek.com)
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...

# ---- USE_MODEL = "gemini-2.5-flash-lite" | "gemini-2.5-flash" -----------
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=...

# ---- USE_MODEL = "qwen3-nothink" | "qwen3-openrouter" | "llama-4-scout" --
# https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Both models are served through OpenRouter, so one key covers both.
# Note: OpenRouter routes to an upstream provider that can change between calls.
#   * llama-4-scout pins novita/bf16 — full precision, never the fp8 endpoint.
#   * qwen3-nothink additionally appends " /no_think" to the system prompt,
#     because reasoning.enabled=False is honoured by SiliconFlow but ignored by
#     DeepInfra. Verify reasoning_tokens ~ 0 after any provider change.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# ---- no key needed ------------------------------------------------------
# USE_MODEL = "mock" runs the whole harness offline, for free, with no API calls.
